The most logic-dense file in the codebase. Highest risk of bugs.

| Function | Edge Cases Missed |
|---|---|
| `startSyncListener` | Listener fires when already connected; NetInfo state has `isInternetReachable: null` (iOS quirk); store has no `profile` or `user`; async race on store import |
| `flushPendingQueue` | **Re-entrancy**: second call while syncing returns `{0, 0}`; Supabase insert succeeds -> deletes report; Supabase returns 23505 (duplicate) -> deletes + increments success; Supabase returns 42501/42P01 -> marks failed; Supabase returns unknown error -> increments failed and **breaks** the loop; inner `catch` -> increments failed and **breaks**; outer `catch` -> returns `{0, -1}`; empty pending queue; 100+ reports (batch boundary) |
| `submitReport` | NetInfo returns `isConnected: true` but `isInternetReachable: false`; Supabase insert succeeds; Supabase returns 23505 -> returns `DUPLICATE_REPORT`; Supabase returns 42501 -> returns `RLS_FORBIDDEN`; Supabase returns other error -> returns error.message; Offline -> calls `db.insertPendingReport` and returns `offline: true`; `db.insertPendingReport` throws |

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The `break` statements inside `flushPendingQueue` on unknown errors create a partial-failure scenario: after a non-triageable error, all remaining reports in the queue are silently skipped. No metric, no retry, no alert. A test surface should validate the "poison message" behavior and decide whether `continue` would be safer than `break`.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

